---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals maintain a system developed by another company?",
    answer:
      "Yes, subject to an initial technical review. We first need to understand the codebase, platform, infrastructure, access and current condition before accepting ongoing responsibility.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do you provide one-time maintenance or only monthly support?",
    answer:
      "Both are possible. Support can be recurring, scheduled, ad-hoc or delivered as a focused improvement project depending on the requirement.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can maintenance include new features?",
    answer:
      "Minor improvements may fit within a maintenance arrangement. Larger features or significant scope changes are normally treated as separate development work so requirements and delivery remain clear.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do you support websites as well as custom software?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Maintenance & Support covers websites, web applications, business software and related technical systems depending on the technology and access available.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "What happens before you take over an existing system?",
    answer:
      "We normally review the existing environment, access, dependencies, hosting, known issues, backups and technical condition before establishing the support arrangement.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can you improve performance without rebuilding the entire system?",
    answer:
      "Often, yes. Performance work begins with diagnosis. Depending on the cause, meaningful improvements may be possible through targeted frontend, backend, database or infrastructure optimisation.",
  },
];
---

<section class="maintenance-faq">
  <div class="site-container maintenance-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Maintenance FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before handing over responsibility.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="maintenance-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .maintenance-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .maintenance-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .maintenance-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .maintenance-faq h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .maintenance-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .maintenance-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .maintenance-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .maintenance-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .maintenance-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
